</div><div mt-section-origin="Courses/Athabasca_University/Chemistry_360:_Organic_Chemistry_II/Chapter_24:_Amines_and_Heterocycles/24.06_Synthesis_of_Amines" class="mt-section" id="section_9"><span id="Amides_can_be_converted_to_1.C2.B0.2C_2.C2.B0_or_3.C2.B0_amines_using_LiAlH4"></span><h2 id="Amides_can_be_converted_to_1.C2.B0.2C_2.C2.B0_or_3.C2.B0_amines_using_LiAlH4-91034">Amides can be converted to 1&deg;, 2&deg; or 3&deg; amines using LiAlH<sub>4</sub></h2>

